    {
      "type": "page",
      "title": "Journal Entry: Into the Woods Character Analysis",
      "href": "https://roundrockisd.schoology.com/page/6582788306",
      "content": "<div class=\"s-page-summary reset s-rte clearfix\"><p style=\"line-height:1.38;text-align:center;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\" dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"font-size:18pt;font-family:'Times New Roman';color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:bold;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap;\">Journal Entry: Character Analysis</span></p>\n<ol style=\"margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;\">\n<li style=\"list-style-type:decimal;font-size:12pt;font-family:'Times New Roman';color:#000000;background-color:transparent;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;\" dir=\"ltr\">\n<p style=\"line-height:1.38;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\" dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt;background-color:transparent;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap;\">Where was your character right before they entered the scene?&nbsp;</span></p>\n</li>\n<li style=\"list-style-type:decimal;font-size:12pt;font-family:'Times New Roman';color:#000000;background-color:transparent;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;\" dir=\"ltr\">\n<p style=\"line-height:1.38;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\" dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt;background-color:transparent;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap;\">Where is your character going next?&nbsp;</span></p>\n</li>\n<li style=\"list-style-type:decimal;font-size:12pt;font-family:'Times New Roman';color:#000000;background-color:transparent;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;\" dir=\"ltr\">\n<p style=\"line-height:1.38;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\" dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt;background-color:transparent;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap;\">How old are they?&nbsp;</span></p>\n</li>\n<li style=\"list-style-type:decimal;font-size:12pt;font-family:'Times New Roman';color:#000000;background-color:transparent;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;\" dir=\"ltr\">\n<p style=\"line-height:1.38;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\" dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt;background-color:transparent;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap;\">What is the thing that your character wants more than anything else? (Objective)</span></p>\n</li>\n<li style=\"list-style-type:decimal;font-size:12pt;font-family:'Times New Roman';color:#000000;background-color:transparent;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;\" dir=\"ltr\">\n<p style=\"line-height:1.38;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\" dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt;background-color:transparent;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap;\">How are they going to get what they want? (Motivation)&nbsp;</span></p>\n</li>\n<li style=\"list-style-type:decimal;font-size:12pt;font-family:'Times New Roman';color:#000000;background-color:transparent;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;\" dir=\"ltr\">\n<p style=\"line-height:1.38;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\" dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt;background-color:transparent;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap;\">What will happen if they don’t get what they want? (Consequence)</span></p>\n</li>\n<li style=\"list-style-type:decimal;font-size:12pt;font-family:'Times New Roman';color:#000000;background-color:transparent;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;\" dir=\"ltr\">\n<p style=\"line-height:1.38;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\" dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt;background-color:transparent;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap;\">What is the social/economic status?&nbsp;</span></p>\n</li>\n<li style=\"list-style-type:decimal;font-size:12pt;font-family:'Times New Roman';color:#000000;background-color:transparent;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;\" dir=\"ltr\">\n<p style=\"line-height:1.38;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\" dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt;background-color:transparent;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap;\">What is their educational level?&nbsp;</span></p>\n</li>\n<li style=\"list-style-type:decimal;font-size:12pt;font-family:'Times New Roman';color:#000000;background-color:transparent;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;\" dir=\"ltr\">\n<p style=\"line-height:1.38;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\" dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt;background-color:transparent;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap;\">Who and/or what is their greatest obstacle?&nbsp;</span></p>\n</li>\n<li style=\"list-style-type:decimal;font-size:12pt;font-family:'Times New Roman';color:#000000;background-color:transparent;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;\" dir=\"ltr\">\n<p style=\"line-height:1.38;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\" dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt;background-color:transparent;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap;\">Who is their greatest ally?&nbsp;</span></p>\n</li>\n<li style=\"list-style-type:decimal;font-size:12pt;font-family:'Times New Roman';color:#000000;background-color:transparent;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;\" dir=\"ltr\">\n<p style=\"line-height:1.38;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\" dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt;background-color:transparent;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap;\">Summarize your character in a single adjective.&nbsp;</span></p>\n</li>\n</ol></div>",
      "images": [],
      "localPath": "Journal Entry_ Into the Woods Character Analysis.html"
    },
    {
      "type": "page",
      "title": "Let's talk about storyboarding",
      "href": "https://roundrockisd.schoology.com/page/6641851076",
      "content": "<div class=\"s-page-summary reset s-rte clearfix\"><p>As we saw in the introduction last class...storyboarding is an essential way that filmakers start to plan out and guide their actions before they shoot any footage.&nbsp; Below I will post some samples of storyboards.&nbsp; Remeber that Storyboards don't have to be works of art.&nbsp; They can simply be stick figures as long as they show you what you need to know about the shot.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;Star Wars</p>\n<p><img src=\"/system/files/attachments/page_embeds/m/2020-09/Storyboard-Examples-for-Film-Storyboard-Ideas-George-Lucas-Star-Wars-A-New-Hope_5f566158a228d.jpg\" alt=\"\" title=\"\"></p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Jurassic Park</p>\n<p><img src=\"/system/files/attachments/page_embeds/m/2020-09/Storyboard-Examples-Storyboard-Ideas-Film-Storyboad-Template-Storyboard-Format-Jurassic-Park_5f56617b764e4.jpg\" alt=\"\" title=\"\"></p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>The Sound of Music</p>\n<p><img src=\"/system/files/attachments/page_embeds/m/2020-09/Storyboard-Examples-for-Film-Storyboard-Ideas-Maurice-Zuberano-Robert-Wise-The-Sound-of-Musi_5f5661939ae09.jpg\" alt=\"\" title=\"\"></p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><iframe src=\"https://www.youtube.com/embed/pLm07s8fnzM?wmode=opaque\" width=\"1000\" height=\"563\" frameborder=\"0\" allowfullscreen=\"\"></iframe></p>\n<p>I have included the link to the clip from the sound of music that fits the storyboard so that you could directly compare how they relate.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Remember that stick figures are okay...here is an example:</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><img src=\"/system/files/attachments/page_embeds/m/2020-09/An-example-of-a-roughly-sketched-storyboard-that-was-provided-to-entrants-of-the-BBCs_5f5662e5e8919.png\" alt=\"\" title=\"\"></p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Next let's take a look at a speific moment in a film and try to storyboard it ourselves.</p></div>",
      "images": [
        "https://roundrockisd.schoology.com/system/files/attachments/page_embeds/m/2020-09/Storyboard-Examples-for-Film-Storyboard-Ideas-George-Lucas-Star-Wars-A-New-Hope_5f566158a228d.jpg",
